Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 7 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M16;
 main's third folder, section 7): FOUR LOCKS COMPARE A NUMBER AS A NUMBER

Four tests fail in a fresh clone on the builder's machine, at main's head and on every patch alike (R80a's
note, section 9): the locks of B1849, B1850 and B1866, and tests/test_b1449_silent_receipts.py. Each compares,
as text, a float or a signed zero that a process printed. Main's word: a lock compares numbers as numbers,
within a stated tolerance, and a zero without its sign.

What each compared:
  - B1849: a whole transcript that holds the size of a commutator that is zero up to rounding, printed to two
    digits (8.4e-16 kept; 6.1e-16 here);
  - B1850: a whole transcript that holds a residual printed the same way (8.5e-15 kept; 2.5e-14 here);
  - B1866: a whole transcript of eighth roots printed with the sign of each part, where a part that is zero
    carries the sign its last operation left on it ("+1-0i" kept; "+1+0i" here). Its comment said that no
    float is compared as text;
  - the test of B1449: one line with an imaginary part that is zero ("+0.00000000j" kept; "-0.00000000j"
    here).

The mend is one small module, scripts/checks/printed_numbers.py, which says its rule: everything that is not
a number is compared character for character; a zero carries no sign; two numbers that are both smaller than
1e-9 in size are the same number; any other two agree to one part in 1e9. The reason for each tolerance is
stated there. Each of the four locks compares by it, with the line it had kept under a dated note.

Its own test, tests/test_printed_numbers.py, holds the four pairs of lines that failed as the same, and holds
twelve changes as different: a count, a group's order, the sign of a number that is not zero, which part of
a number is zero, the sign of a real part, the seventh digit, a residual that is no residual, a word, a
ratio, an order of pairs, a number that is missing, a whole number that is not one.

What it does not do, said in the module: it does not say that a number is right, only that two transcripts
give the same one.

Run on this machine: the four locks' files, 16 tests. On the commit before: 4 failed, 12 passed. On the
patch: 16 passed, and the 3 tests of the module. Not run on main's machine.

Main's word for the rule; the tolerances are the builder's choice and are main's to change.
